vitaGL (LGPL-3.0-or-later) — read this before publishing a binary

  Source:  https://github.com/Rinnegatamante/vitaGL
  Build:   linked from the prebuilt archive in VitaSDK, vdpm package
           `vitaGL 0.0.0.r1488.g2bdbe89-1` (arm-vita-eabi/lib/libvitaGL.a), from the
           stable `2026.08` package channel (sequence 2026111076)
  Licence: LGPL version 3 or later, as stated in its source headers. Its licence texts are NOT
           reproduced here because no vitaGL source is included in this repository.

  This is the one place where the licence position needs care. vitaGL is LGPL, and LGPL requires that
  a user be able to modify it and relink the application against the modified library. Today this
  port links an opaque prebuilt archive that comes from a different build than any clearly identified
  source revision, so that relink right cannot be demonstrated from this repository alone.

  Before any binary release that links vitaGL, do one of the following:

    1. Build vitaGL from a named source revision inside this project and link that archive, keeping
       the source, the build recipe and any local patches here, so the relink is reproducible. This is
       the approach used by https://github.com/NathanKneT/DuskOnVita (pinned archive plus SHA-256 in
       deps.lock, patches in patches/deps/vitagl/), and it is the recommended fix.
    2. Otherwise, ship the archive as a separate replaceable file plus a written offer of the
       corresponding source and link instructions, and say so in the release notes.

  Until one of those is done, treat this repository as source-only and do not publish a VPK.

Sony and Nintendo material — never included

  This repository contains no game disc image, no extracted game data, no Nintendo or Sony software,
  and no shader compiler. In particular `libshacccg.suprx` is never copied or bundled; each user
  extracts it from their own console to ur0:data/. Users supply their own legally obtained disc image.

